• Optional account: sign in under Settings and your progress and training settings sync across your iPhone, iPad, Mac, Android and PC.
• A new on-screen key on every keying screen. It keys each touch the moment it lands, even inside scrolling screens, two-finger paddle squeezes still work, and pulling down Control Center mid-press no longer leaves the key stuck down. The sidetone plays the exact pitch you set and answers sooner.
• MIDI paddles timed by the app: a Vail Adapter in Passthrough or an N6ARA TinyMIDI now keys iambic at your Paddle mode and speed. A Morserino-32 straight key (MIDI note 30) works too.
• Daily Dit: Past puzzles plays the last 30 days as practice, and each guess row shows the speed you actually heard.
• Key to continue after a miss in Journey, Type It and QRQ Speed. New "Short callsigns only (4 characters)" option for Pileup, Contest and Rapid Fire.
• When a timed session runs out, the drill on screen waits for your answer.
• Drill and game sounds take turns instead of cutting into each other; CW Galaga paces enemies so every one is heard; smoother arcade frames; Brass Knuckles holds a phone in portrait.
• Fixes: Listen timer while paused, the Bluetooth key sheet on iOS 27.
• Also new since build 41: Brass Knuckles Knock Out (Games), the Daily DiDaaaaahDit and the POTA hunt simulator.
Please try: signing in on two devices and changing a setting on one; fast taps, squeezes and Control Center mid-press on the on-screen key; a MIDI paddle; and a few waves of CW Galaga.
